{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836296",
      "title": "Introducing Refs: Connecting & Accessing HTML Elements via Refs",
      "sourceHash": "337aafc4edc1c2bd12fb1fff228c3641df5d377b5125fa94f0855ba2e98c9a95",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 1.92,
          "en": "So what are refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.92,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "and how can we simplify this component with refs?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 8.25,
          "en": "Well, a ref in React is a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.25,
          "end": 10.95,
          "en": "just as the state in the end is a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.95,
          "end": 13.835,
          "en": "and just as a variable contains a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.835,
          "end": 16.717,
          "en": "but it's a special kind of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.717,
          "end": 21.24,
          "en": "or it's managed by React in a special way to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.24,
          "end": 24.72,
          "en": "Now you can create such a ref value in React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.72,
          "end": 28.599,
          "en": "by importing the use ref hook from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.599,
          "end": 31.56,
          "en": "So another built-in hook function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.56,
          "end": 33.9,
          "en": "which like all hook functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.9,
          "end": 36.983,
          "en": "must be called inside of a Component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.983,
          "end": 39.46,
          "en": "or inside of a custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.46,
          "end": 41.883,
          "en": "but that's something we'll explore later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "You then create a ref value like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "and you can store it in a constant or variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 49.38,
          "en": "and give it any name you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 52.955,
          "en": "Now here I will create a ref value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.955,
          "end": 56.55,
          "en": "to, in the end, get the value that will be entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.55,
          "end": 58.71,
          "en": "into this input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 63.3,
          "en": "And therefore, I'll name it input or player name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.3,
          "end": 65.388,
          "en": "The name here, of course, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.388,
          "end": 70.02,
          "en": "And whilst you can do more with these ref values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 72.12,
          "en": "and later in the section you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.12,
          "end": 74.25,
          "en": "what you can do more with them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.25,
          "end": 76.08,
          "en": "one thing you can do with them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.08,
          "end": 78.48,
          "en": "and one thing you will probably do the most",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.48,
          "end": 81.191,
          "en": "with those refs is that you can connect them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.191,
          "end": 83.768,
          "en": "to JSX elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.768,
          "end": 87.389,
          "en": "And you can do that with a special prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.389,
          "end": 91.11,
          "en": "that's supported by all React Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.11,
          "end": 94.42699999999999,
          "en": "automatically out of the box, the ref prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.42699999999999,
          "end": 98.844,
          "en": "which just like the key prop is a special prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.844,
          "end": 103.02000000000001,
          "en": "Now React takes such a ref value as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.02000000000001,
          "end": 106.864,
          "en": "so in my case, my player name like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.864,
          "end": 111.47999999999999,
          "en": "and with that, this input component here is in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.47999999999999,
          "end": 112.923,
          "en": "connected to this ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.55799999999999,
          "end": 116.64,
          "en": "Now how does this connection help us though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.64,
          "end": 120.33,
          "en": "Well, we can now use this ref value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.33,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "for example, in handle click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 124.59,
          "en": "so when this button here is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.59,
          "end": 128.253,
          "en": "to access the underlying connected element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.21,
          "end": 133.65,
          "en": "so through player name we can access this input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.65,
          "end": 136.11,
          "en": "because player name is connected to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.11,
          "end": 137.313,
          "en": "through the ref prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.96,
          "end": 141.81,
          "en": "Therefore, here in handle click, we can get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.81,
          "end": 143.28,
          "en": "to the input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.28,
          "end": 146.88,
          "en": "though it's worth noting that for all these ref values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.88,
          "end": 149.94,
          "en": "created with useRef, you first have to access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.94,
          "end": 152.058,
          "en": "a current property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.058,
          "end": 156.9,
          "en": "So this ref value you are getting back from useRef",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.9,
          "end": 161.9,
          "en": "will always, really always be a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.85399999999998,
          "end": 166.421,
          "en": "that will always have a current property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.421,
          "end": 170.084,
          "en": "and only a current property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.084,
          "end": 173.25,
          "en": "And it's then in this current property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.25,
          "end": 176.1,
          "en": "that the actual ref value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.1,
          "end": 179.403,
          "en": "so in this case, the connected input will be stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.78,
          "end": 183.18,
          "en": "Therefore now current, in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.18,
          "end": 186.49,
          "en": "holds this input element as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.5,
          "end": 190.47,
          "en": "and therefore even though I'm not getting auto suggestion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.47,
          "end": 192.48,
          "en": "for it here, because my IDE",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.48,
          "end": 195.15,
          "en": "doesn't fully understand this connection here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.15,
          "end": 197.46,
          "en": "I can now access all the methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.46,
          "end": 199.86,
          "en": "and properties that are exposed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.86,
          "end": 202.82999999999998,
          "en": "by that input HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.82999999999998,
          "end": 207.82999999999998,
          "en": "And I really mean the built-in Native input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.26,
          "end": 211.86,
          "en": "On MDN, you can learn all about its methods that are exposed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.86,
          "end": 213.78,
          "en": "and all the properties that are exposed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.78,
          "end": 217.05,
          "en": "and you can access all these properties and methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.05,
          "end": 220.293,
          "en": "through the ref here, which is connected to this element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.43,
          "end": 223.68,
          "en": "And therefore here we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.68,
          "end": 225.66,
          "en": "access the value property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.66,
          "end": 228.573,
          "en": "which holds the currently entered value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.44,
          "end": 231.69,
          "en": "And we could now use that to update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.69,
          "end": 234.403,
          "en": "our entered player name state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.403,
          "end": 239.34,
          "en": "so in handle click we could now call set entered player name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.34,
          "end": 240.85,
          "en": "to update that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.92,
          "end": 244.47,
          "en": "and pass this value which we're getting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.47,
          "end": 247.803,
          "en": "directly from the input field as a value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.12,
          "end": 252.6,
          "en": "And therefore we don't have to log that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.6,
          "end": 255.12,
          "en": "on every keystroke anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.12,
          "end": 257.888,
          "en": "Instead, we can get rid of the handle change function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.888,
          "end": 261.27,
          "en": "get rid of the submitted state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.27,
          "end": 264.67,
          "en": "and just keep the ref and the entered player name state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.98,
          "end": 270.98,
          "en": "and down there also get rid of the unchanged prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 271.14,
          "end": 275.58,
          "en": "and of the value prop here, we don't need all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 275.58,
          "end": 277.383,
          "en": "The ref is enough instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.64,
          "end": 281.55,
          "en": "And up here we therefore now just want to check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 281.55,
          "end": 284.97,
          "en": "if entered player name is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.97,
          "end": 288.12,
          "en": "so if it's not an empty string, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.12,
          "end": 290.52,
          "en": "in which case we want to output it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 290.52,
          "end": 292.743,
          "en": "Otherwise we output unknown entity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 294.09000000000003,
          "end": 296.46,
          "en": "And for return expressions like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 296.46,
          "end": 298.92,
          "en": "there is a shortcut in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.92,
          "end": 301.44,
          "en": "You can simply write two question marks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.44,
          "end": 303.614,
          "en": "and with that you are telling JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.614,
          "end": 306.36,
          "en": "that it should output this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.36,
          "end": 311.36,
          "en": "if it's truthy or this value if it's falsey.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.52,
          "end": 314.733,
          "en": "So if entered player name is an empty string, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 316.68,
          "end": 318.66,
          "en": "But with that we're now updating the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 318.66,
          "end": 321.09,
          "en": "only on a click and we're getting the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 321.09,
          "end": 324.363,
          "en": "directly from the input element with help of that ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 326.07,
          "end": 327.828,
          "en": "Therefore, now if we save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 327.828,
          "end": 331.023,
          "en": "and we go back to this application and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 331.98,
          "end": 335.069,
          "en": "if I enter Max, nothing happens on every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.069,
          "end": 338.823,
          "en": "but if I click set name, it's output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 339.93,
          "end": 342.75,
          "en": "And if I now continue typing, nothing happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 342.75,
          "end": 343.58299999999997,
          "en": "which is great,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 343.58299999999997,
          "end": 346.203,
          "en": "but if it clicks that name again, it's updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 347.22,
          "end": 351.39,
          "en": "And that's one of the reasons why this ref feature exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 351.39,
          "end": 355.59000000000003,
          "en": "For use cases like this where you just wanna read a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.59000000000003,
          "end": 357.65999999999997,
          "en": "from an input field, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 357.65999999999997,
          "end": 360,
          "en": "it can really save you a lot of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 360,
          "end": 362.283,
          "en": "and lead to leaner Components.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}